WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.205 --> 00:00:02.880
What lies between a gut microbe and a health outcome?

2
00:00:03.285 --> 00:00:05.914
BiomeTrail opens that hidden journey,

3
00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:08.910
from microbial molecules through host receptors

4
00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:11.180
and pathways to health outcomes.

5
00:00:11.558 --> 00:00:15.471
It organizes over two hundred forty thousand PubMed records,

6
00:00:15.574 --> 00:00:18.909
keeping source sentences and experimental conditions attached.

7
00:00:19.283 --> 00:00:22.652
Ask a question, and AI traces the evidence.

8
00:00:22.859 --> 00:00:24.515
In a twenty-two-question benchmark,

9
00:00:24.595 --> 00:00:28.115
ninety-four point four percent of cited claims were supported.

10
00:00:28.522 --> 00:00:30.467
Across ten mechanism questions,

11
00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:33.338
it recovered one hundred supported intermediates,

12
00:00:33.545 --> 00:00:36.185
versus twenty-six with PubMed retrieval.

13
00:00:36.591 --> 00:00:38.849
Conflicting findings stay visible.

14
00:00:39.079 --> 00:00:41.638
These cross-study chains remain hypotheses,

15
00:00:41.787 --> 00:00:43.872
with every step open to inspection.

16
00:00:44.293 --> 00:00:47.974
BiomeTrail. Follow the evidence, preserve the context,

17
00:00:48.077 --> 00:00:49.386
and see what to test next.
